      "message": "We have no idea why these two patches were not applied together.\n\nTwo patches uploaded together.\n[PATCH 0/2] ALSA: Clear PCM buffers more properly\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/all/20201218145625.2045-1-tiwai@suse.de/\n\nPatch number 1 missed in K5.10\n[PATCH 1/2] ALSA: memalloc: Align buffer allocations in page size\n+\tsize \u003d PAGE_ALIGN(size);\n\nOnly patch number 2 applied in K5.10\n[PATCH 2/2] ALSA: pcm: Clear the full allocated memory at hw_params\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/all/20201218145625.2045-3-tiwai@suse.de/ \n+\t\tif (runtime-\u003einfo \u0026 SNDRV_PCM_INFO_MMAP)\n+\t\t\tsize \u003d PAGE_ALIGN(size);\n+\t\tmemset(runtime-\u003edma_area, 0, size);\n\nKasan gets a vmalloc-out-of-bounds problem.\nClearly allocation and initialization size of this dma buffer mismatch.\nSo we think these two patches should be applied together\n(In newer kernel version, two patches were both merged.)\n\nKasan log\n[  893.445287] [T500674] HwBinder:636_1: [name:report\u0026]\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\n[  893.445351] [T500674] HwBinder:636_1: [name:report\u0026]BUG: KASAN: vmalloc-out-of-bounds in snd_pcm_hw_params+0xa50/0x1184\n[  893.445381] [T500674] HwBinder:636_1: [name:report\u0026]Write of size 8192 at addr ffffffd04383d000 by task HwBinder:636_1/674\n[  893.445400] [T500674] HwBinder:636_1: [name:report\u0026]\n[  893.445431] [T500674] HwBinder:636_1: CPU: 5 PID: 674 Comm: HwBinder:636_1 Tainted: G S      W  O      5.10.43-android12-9-g33642899f091 #1\n[  893.445450] [T500674] HwBinder:636_1: Hardware name: MT6983(ENG) (DT)\n[  893.445467] [T500674] HwBinder:636_1: Call trace:\n[  893.445